{
  "observed_defect": "The current source terrain is flat and lacks the necessary organic relief to support a player city, with no sculpted gully or crest to enhance the visual depth. The Breach edge in the northeast is not properly defined and appears as a flat, unconnected surface, failing to create a coherent silhouette and architectural continuity. The player city is positioned on a flat plane with no visible ground contact or elevation, making it difficult to integrate with the surrounding environment.",
  "design_intent": "To create a physically sculpted Breach edge in the northeast, with a broad asymmetric gully and a weathered crest to improve relief, while preserving the outside sector boundaries for later joining. The goal is to achieve a cohesive, legible fantasy-medieval world with a strategy-camera legibility that emphasizes architectural intent and surface/material depth.",
